 "response": "Kifux's budget is now **$680K**.\n\n**How the rules were applied**\n- Only Finance Office records changed the budget. Marketing, Legal, Vendor, Operations and other messages were ignored. So were Finance notes that do not change the budget, such as audits, invoices and room moves.\n- A withdrawn update counts as if it never happened. Where a withdrawal was itself withdrawn, I followed the chain from the latest record backwards. For example:\n  - #0887 voids #0528, so #0375 stays in force. #0375 voids #0226, which leaves #0213 in force. #0213 voids #0146, leaving #0134 in force. #0134 voids #0075, so the $434K cut in #0005 still applies.\n  - #0837 voids #0699, leaving #0422 in force. #0422 voids #0258, leaving #0006 in force, so #0003 (the $461K cut) is withdrawn.\n  - #1271 voids #1241, leaving #1227 in force, so #0448 (the $248K cut) is withdrawn.\n  - #1318 voids #0978, leaving #0976 in force. #0976 voids #0324, so the $443K cut in #0186 still applies.\n- In total, about 110 budget updates end up withdrawn and were left out.\n\n**Result**\nStarting from the $2,070K set in #0001, I applied every remaining Finance Office change once, in order, through #1599. I did this as a single running total and did not do a separate second check of the arithmetic.\n\nANSWER: $680K",
